message.content:
This looks like a CBP ruling on orthodontic wire bending machines. The likely candidates are 8463.30 (machines for working wire) or 9018.49 (dental instruments and appliances), and I believe CBP chose 8463.30.0000.

Heading 8463 covers other machine tools for working metal without removing material, and 8463.30 is specifically for machines for working wire. Chapter 90 Note 1(f) excludes the articles of heading 8463 from the chapter, but 9018 covers dental instruments. Since the machine is a wire-bending machine and not a hand instrument, 8463.30.0000 is the best fit. Note that heading 8463 machines are not "machine tools" in the sense of heading 8456-8465 being limited to a single use. The Section XVI note also gives the wire-bending function priority, and the 8463.30.0000 subheading has a single statistical suffix.

{"hts_code": "8463.30.0000", "reason": "The machines bend wire into shapes by automated means, so they are machines for working wire of heading 8463 (other machine tools for working metal without removing material), not dental instruments of heading 9018."}
